h-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1ef91f19e7f4c6033e23b9c6c0b91143e5cb5ede269d129cb1c0006e5f2569ec","event_uuid":"0bf474a8-3f1d-4d22-a1da-f61aa2841b24","position":{"commit_sha":"b78f9bb445435c33ca9bda978f38d22cf914b291","position":"1785531821764036001-0bf474a8-3f1d-4d22-a1da-f61aa2841b24"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"82fdf26e2abe78a518b10a4d7d10cf9d4dc750d9e6160b639c117c244dcd8ba6","event_uuid":"5bb3cd6f-3ce0-4f72-b834-963240a09a2a","position":{"commit_sha":"3cf255f697c007f587fa85d844f0576bf5f37167","position":"1785543440269468001-5bb3cd6f-3ce0-4f72-b834-963240a09a2a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785531615531498001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f1dffb55-45cf-4c13-9940-323dc1de4c8d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"77e1-7f82-98e6-4fed"},{"link_uuid":"808727f7-8b7f-4867-8842-1531d486d17e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"01e8-302b-ab8f-4220"},{"link_uuid":"5bb3cd6f-3ce0-4f72-b834-963240a09a2a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9305-b42c-3262-4c58"}],"description":"Split out of task 77e1-7f82-98e6-4fed (dominant-northbound-blackrhino) so that ticket can close honestly against the scope it actually delivered.\n\n## BLOCKED — do not start until bug 01e8-302b-ab8f-4220 closes\n\nBug 01e8 (\"rebar init bootstrapped a fresh empty tracker while origin/tickets already existed\") is IN PROGRESS in another session covering store/init/sync divergence, and has already modified `src/rebar/_commands/init.py` and the fsck path. 01e8 declares NO `file_impact`, so the overlap with the two call sites below cannot be verified precisely. Rather than guess and risk a conflicting edit to a file another session holds, the operator deferred these two sites into this ticket.\n\n**Unblock condition:** 01e8 reaches `closed`. Re-read both call sites at that point — 01e8 may have moved, rewritten, or already bounded them, exactly as it turned out for `_ref_lock.py` under 77e1 (see below).\n\n## The two deferred sites\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/init.py` — `fetch <remote> <branch>` (~line 375)\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py` — `push origin HEAD:tickets` (~line 338)\n\nBoth are network-capable git subprocess calls that can block indefinitely on a stuck remote or a hung credential helper. Line numbers are from the 77e1 sweep and may have drifted — locate by command, not by line.\n\n## Precedent to follow (already established; do not invent a new mechanism)\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py:57` and `src/rebar/_store/sync.py:58` — `_GIT_TIMEOUT = 30`, for INCREMENTAL ref-sized ops against an already-warm clone.\n- `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py` — `_GIT_TIMEOUT = 300` (added by bug 747f, merged as `96a0d5c3f`), for a COLD materializing fetch that is legitimately minutes.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py` and `src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py` — bounded under 77e1 itself; read that change as the nearest reference implementation.\n\nPick the value by call profile, not by habit: `fsck_repair`'s `push origin HEAD:tickets` is an incremental push of ticket events against a warm clone, so the 30s `_store` precedent fits it. `init`'s `fetch <remote> <branch>` is a cold first fetch into a freshly-initialised store and can legitimately take minutes, so the 300s `_snapshot` precedent fits it. Justify whichever you choose.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Both call sites above pass an explicit timeout, with a comment justifying the value against the cited precedent.\n2. A timeout surfaces as an ACTIONABLE error naming the git operation that timed out and the bound it exceeded — never a bare `subprocess.TimeoutExpired` and never a hang. Follow the `_store/push.py` synthetic-`CompletedProcess(124)` precedent or the module's own existing error type, whichever fits the call site.\n3. A held-out RED->GREEN test proves the timeout is passed AND that a timing-out call produces the descriptive error rather than propagating `TimeoutExpired`.\n4. `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the default suite exit zero.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/init.py","reason":"bound the fetch <remote> <branch> call site with an explicit timeout"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py","reason":"bound the push origin HEAD:tickets call site with an explicit timeout"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","01e8-302b-ab8f-4220"],["relates_to","9305-b42c-3262-4c58"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"983f-ee85-1e06-428e","ticket_type":"task","title":"Bound the two _commands/ network-capable git call sites with an explicit timeout","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b33dd0a5-86b1-40a1-8786-585b02566a05","f1dffb55-45cf-4c13-9940-323dc1de4c8d","808727f7-8b7f-4867-8842-1531d486d17e","0bf474a8-3f1d-4d22-a1da-f61aa2841b24","5bb3cd6f-3ce0-4f72-b834-963240a09a2a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785543440269468002,"uuid":"e40de7dd-2b91-4d02-bdab-1116f911973e"}